-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification of the main game's hooks on
              three recordings; the hand-over from the front end and the level
              blocks from memory by unit cases and a recording's real tape
              load; simulated boot of both builds; run in OverSpec from the
              title into level 1, one and two players. Played by the owner on
              a ZX Spectrum Next (KS3), 2026-11-27: good.

  Replay      NexClash differential verification of the main game's hooks on
              the rzxarchive's recordings of level blocks 1, 2 and 10 (61,548
              frames, 11,502 updates): every register and all game memory
              after each hook, the tile layer against the painted map after
              every update -> IDENTICAL. Level block 1 from memory equal to a
              recording's real tape load. The hand-over from the front end to
              the main game: unit case, and one broken build detected.

  Emulator    OverSpec: from the title through the heroes' and controls
              screens into level 1, one and two players, scripted keys

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: played by
              the owner, good

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
